				<section class="elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-dd659e2 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default" data-id="dd659e2" data-element_type="section" data-e-type="section" data-settings="{&quot;_ha_eqh_enable&quot;:false}">
						<div class="elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default">
					<div class="elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-a758164" data-id="a758164" data-element_type="column" data-e-type="column">
			<div class="elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated">
						<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-ae34de5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="ae34de5" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<h4 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 13pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #ead1dc; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">COMPLICATIONS OF MALARIA</span><b id="docs-internal-guid-1c4520a0-7fff-32bb-fbb2-9f541d7a20ca" style="font-weight: normal;"></b></h4><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Effects on Pregnancy:</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> </span></p><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #d9ead3; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">To the mother:</span></p><ul><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Increased Risk of Severe Malaria</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Pregnancy significantly increases the susceptibility to severe malaria, putting mothers at higher risk of complications like cerebral malaria, pulmonary edema, and renal failure.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">High Temperatures</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Fever associated with malaria can cause intense discomfort and dehydration, particularly for pregnant women who are already experiencing hormonal changes and increased body temperature.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Anaemia</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Malaria parasites destroy red blood cells, leading to anaemia, which can be exacerbated during pregnancy when blood volume increases. Severe anaemia can lead to fatigue, weakness, and shortness of breath, further jeopardizing the mother&#8217;s health.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Puerperal and Cerebral Malaria</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: These life-threatening conditions pose a high risk to pregnant women. Puerperal malaria occurs during or after childbirth, while cerebral malaria involves the brain and can lead to coma and death.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Antepartum and Postpartum Haemorrhage</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Malaria increases the risk of bleeding before or after childbirth, leading to severe blood loss and potential complications for both mother and baby.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Ill Health and Compromised Immunity:</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> Malaria symptoms, including nausea, vomiting, diarrhoea, and loss of appetite, can affect a pregnant woman&#8217;s health and worsen nutritional deficiencies. The weakened immune system makes her more susceptible to infections.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Jaundice and Dehydration:</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> The buildup of bilirubin, a breakdown product of red blood cells, can cause jaundice, which further compromises the mother&#8217;s health and can impact the baby&#8217;s development. Dehydration, a common symptom of malaria, can lead to complications for both the mother and fetus.</span></li></ul><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #d9ead3; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">To the baby:</span></p><ul><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Abortions</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Malaria increases the risk of miscarriage, especially during the first trimester.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Prematurity</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Malaria can trigger premature labor, leading to babies born before 37 weeks of pregnancy, increasing their risk of health problems.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Intrauterine Fetal Death (IUFD)</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Malaria can lead to the death of the baby in the womb, especially in the third trimester.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Low Birth Weight:</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> Babies born to mothers with malaria are more likely to have low birth weight, increasing their risk of health problems and long-term developmental issues.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Congenital Malaria:</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> The baby can be infected with malaria parasites in the womb, leading to complications at birth or later in life.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Intrauterine Growth Restriction (IUGR):</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> Malaria can hinder the baby&#8217;s growth in the womb, leading to smaller size at birth, impacting their long-term health and development.</span></li></ul><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Effects on the Ward:</span></p><ul><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Extended Hospital Stays</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Malaria complications can lead to prolonged hospital stays, burdening healthcare resources and increasing the risk of infections.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Blockage of Space for Urgent Obstetric Cases</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Long stays by malaria patients can limit space and resources for urgent obstetric cases, delaying critical care for other mothers.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Ward Congestion and Cross-Infection</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Overcrowding due to malaria cases can increase the risk of cross-infection, affecting the health of other patients and healthcare workers.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Financial Strain on Families</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Treatment and hospitalization for malaria can strain the finances of families, especially in developing countries where access to healthcare is limited.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Deprivation of Maternal Care for Children at Home</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Mothers hospitalized for malaria are unable to care for their other children, potentially leading to neglect and health issues.</span></li><li dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.38;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: #fff2cc; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; -webkit-text-decoration-skip: none; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Economic Inefficiency</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Poppins,sans-serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">: Malaria during pregnancy not only affects individual families but also impacts economic productivity due to lost work days, reduced income, and increased healthcare costs.</span></li></ul>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
		</div>
					</div>
		</section>
				<section class="elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-406eefc elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default" data-id="406eefc" data-element_type="section" data-e-type="section" data-settings="{&quot;_ha_eqh_enable&quot;:false}">
						<div class="elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default">
					<div class="elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-8d44718" data-id="8d44718" data-element_type="column" data-e-type="column">
			<div class="elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated">
						<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-ed95834 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="ed95834" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<script async src="https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=ca-pub-5767364969818632"
     crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
<ins class="adsbygoogle"
     style="display:block"
