			</item>
		<item>
		<title>EPILEPSY IN PREGNANCY</title>
		<link>https://midwivesrevisionuganda.com/epilepsy-in-pregnancy/</link>
					<comments>https://midwivesrevisionuganda.com/epilepsy-in-pregnancy/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[midwivesrevision@gmail.com]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 15 Jan 2025 06:37:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Uncategorised]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://midwivesrevisionuganda.com/?p=7036</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[EPILEPSY IN PREGNANCY Epilepsy is a chronic disorder characterized by recurrent, unpredictable seizures due to temporary dysfunction of the brain&#8217;s neurons producing excessive electrical discharge.  Although it typically presents in childhood, it has a second peak in older adults, with women of childbearing age accounting for 23% of those affected. The prevalence of epilepsy in [&#8230;]]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[		<div data-elementor-type="wp-post" data-elementor-id="7036" class="elementor elementor-7036" data-elementor-settings="{&quot;ha_cmc_init_switcher&quot;:&quot;no&quot;}">
						<section class="elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-fe73d7c elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default" data-id="fe73d7c" data-element_type="section" data-e-type="section" data-settings="{&quot;_ha_eqh_enable&quot;:false}">
